# F1 (SOFT, card M only, FIRST of the card-M jobs): the conv-gates spread launch against the served gdn_decode_conv_gates, bit for bit, on one card (optimisation/ttnn-op/gdn_conv_gates_spread). Cases 16, 64 and 128 rows, random and edge data (+-0, denormals, the smallest normal, the largest finite), two seeds each:
# conv, beta, g and the four advanced windows compared as int16 bit patterns, plus the core plan of each case; then, only after a PASS, the timing (24 launches per round, 25 serpentine rounds, per-launch median and quartiles of each arm).
# WHY FIRST AND WHY ON CARD M: the two new kernels (gdn_conv_gates_spread_reader.cpp and _writer.cpp) were never compiled before this run (the session that wrote them had no toolchain): a JIT compile error, a hang or a differing byte shows here in minutes instead of three hours into A1. The timing (each arm under a captured trace of 24 launches, so the host's program-descriptor build is not in it) also settles how long a conv core takes
# (the launch's floor is the slower of its conv cores and its gate cores) at 16, 64 and 128 rows, which P1 can only read at 64.
# ONE CARD SEES ONE CHIP: whether the four chips of a mesh agree is A1's audit (every chip). READ: 'GDN_CG_SPREAD verdict=PASS' (exit 0), every compare differing=0 fell_back=False, then the timing lines (spread_us against served_us per case; the plan says about -18 to -21 us at 64 rows). FAIL names the tensor and the count; NOT-RUN carries the error text (a compile error is there verbatim).
# A FAIL or a NOT-RUN here does not stop the window (this job is soft) but A1 then runs F1 knowing it: read it before A1, and THE FALLBACK IS COMMITTED: if F1 is FAIL or NOT-RUN, run every later job that names c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2 or c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2-audit (A1, H1-H5, T2, T5, T8, P1) on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2-nof1 or c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2-nof1-audit (wave 1 plus the multi-user SDPA launch, no F1), by that one C2_PROFILE swap in the template: the profiles are in this image, so no new commit and no new image (ORDER.txt, F1 FALLBACK). Duration (estimate): 20 min (container timeout 1 h; the per-call watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the card is resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# CARD M ONLY, BEFORE ANY QUAD JOB: the cardm step runs one board; it never runs while a quad step holds the cards, and the harness refuses while anything else can reach the board.
# The harness's container turns the image's C2 boot hook off (QWEN_C2_SERVING=0) and unsets the baked four-card mesh descriptor (env -u TT_MESH_GRAPH_DESC_PATH); the workflow's
# cardm step waits for other CI's buildx builders instead of refusing the window. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is the image B0 built (a harness mounts this checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs).
C2_SUPERSEDED_BY=tp4-w2ln-jobs
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/gdn_conv_gates_spread/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
